I start protecting items later than some folks and I'm more selective
about which items to protect.  The scrolls usually found in Sokoban are
not ones used by monsters in combat and few monsters eat to food items
found on the floor in Sokoban.  As a result I'm not much interested in
covering them.

For me locking items in a chest comes later in the game and then I'm
more selective.  For most levels I'll pile all non-rock items near the
stairs.  Then I'll selectively take the interesting ones with me until I
have so much I build a cache level.  There I will fill a chest with
artifacts, wands and other items that monsters will use in combat.

I only shuttle all items to each level if I plan on doing a polypile.


